@title Late Sales Dashboards Postmortem
@subtitle Daily sales dashboards 9 hours late, Juniper Retail
@author Analytics Platform
@date 2026-10-02

## Impact

- 9 hours of delay (normally ready by 02:00, refreshed at 10:58).
- 23 dashboards stale.
- The 08:00 executive sales report went out with the previous day's numbers.

## Pipeline

diagram pipe dir=LR title="Nightly sales pipeline"
pipe: ordersdb "Orders DB" db
pipe: cdc "CDC Connector" svc
pipe: kafka "Kafka" queue
pipe: spark "Spark Job" fn "failed: out of memory" focus
pipe: warehouse "Warehouse" store
pipe: dash "Dashboards" ext
pipe: ordersdb -> cdc -> kafka
pipe: kafka -> spark : orders topic
pipe: spark -> warehouse -> dash

## Timeline

table = Time,Event; 01:00,Nightly Spark Job starts; 01:47,Spark Job fails with out-of-memory on the orders partition for 2026-10-01; 02:30,Automatic retry also fails; 07:55,Analyst reports stale dashboards; 08:20,On-call doubles executor memory to 16 GB and reruns; 10:05,Spark Job succeeds; 10:58,Dashboards refreshed

## Root cause

A promotion on 2026-10-01 produced 3.4 times the normal order volume: 4.1 million orders against a typical 1.2 million. The Spark Job's executors had 8 GB of memory each, sized for normal days, so the job ran out of memory on that day's orders partition. The automatic retry used the same settings and failed the same way, and nobody was paged, so the failure sat unnoticed until an analyst reported stale data.

## Lessons learned

### What went well

- Once on-call was engaged, the fix (doubling executor memory) was found and applied within 25 minutes.
- The rerun completed cleanly and dashboards refreshed without data loss.

### What did not go well

- Two consecutive failures paged no one; the problem was found by an analyst six hours later.
- Executor memory was fixed, not sized from input volume.
- Dashboards gave no sign that their data was stale.

## Action items

1. Page on-call when the nightly job fails twice.
2. Size executor memory from the input volume.
3. Add a data freshness banner to dashboards.
